---
config:
  flowchart:
    wrappingWidth: 400
---
flowchart TB
    accTitle: How a diagram reaches every reader
    accDescr: A diagram is a Mermaid source in docs/diagrams/. scripts/diagrams.sh draws it with mermaid-cli in Docker as an SVG picture for the light and one for the dark theme, which the Markdown shows with a picture element, so that the GitHub app, the stores, e-mails and github.com all show it. The website draws the source itself, live. In a pull request that changes a diagram, the check diagrams draws the pictures anew, and the diagram bot commits those that differ.

    you(["You"])
    source["`**docs/diagrams/NAME.mmd**<br>Mermaid, from top to bottom<br>accTitle · accDescr`"]
    draw["scripts/diagrams.sh<br>mermaid-cli in Docker<br>without network"]
    pictures["docs/images/diagrams/<br>NAME.svg · NAME.dark.svg"]
    readers["README and docs/ with a picture<br>the GitHub app · github.com<br>HACS · App Store · PyPI · e-mails"]
    website["The website<br>draws the source live"]
    check{"The check diagrams:<br>the same pictures?"}
    bot(["Diagram bot<br>commits the pictures"])

    you -- "writes" --> source
    source --> draw --> pictures --> readers
    source -- "the hook of MkDocs" --> website
    source -. "a pull request" .-> check
    check -- "no, on a branch<br>of the repository" --> bot
    bot -.-> pictures

    classDef bot fill:#526cfe2e,stroke:#526cfe,stroke-width:2px
    classDef person fill:#f59e0b2e,stroke:#f59e0b,stroke-width:2px
    classDef done fill:#16a34a2e,stroke:#16a34a,stroke-width:2px
    class draw,check,bot bot
    class you,source person
    class readers,website done
